      "output": "Implemented both methods.\n\n`GetOrder` (`fetch/client.go:62`) does a bounded retry loop: 2xx decodes the order, other 4xx is `ErrRejected`, and 5xx/429/transport failures are retried up to `Attempts` with backoff starting at `Pause` and growing each time, treating a valid `Retry-After` as a floor. Exhausted attempts or a bad response produce `ErrUnavailable` naming the id; a cancelled ctx returns `ctx.Err()`.\n\n`PlaceOrder` (`fetch/orders.go:25`) sends the documented POST **once** — the doc's warning that the partner records the order before answering makes replay unsafe — then maps 4xx≠429 to `ErrRejected` and 5xx/429/transport to `ErrUnavailable`, naming the sku. JSON uses `encoding/json/v2` (Go 1.27 idiom). Retry-After parsing lives in `retryAfter`.\n\nAdded `fetch/fetch_contract_test.go` covering success, rejection, retry counts, Retry-After, cancellation, and the no-replay rule for POST.\n\n```text\nchecks: gofmt pass · vet pass · test -race pass · golangci-lint pass (0 issues) · go fix -diff clean\nadded package-level declarations: 1 — retryAfter: GetOrder\n```"
